    "The compound's SMILES suggests a polyphenolic/lactone-like structure; potential assay interference (luminescence quenching, aggregation, redox activity) should be checked via the compound-only blank and, if suspected, an orthogonal readout.",
    "If inhibition is ATP-competitive, IC50 depends on ATP concentration relative to Km; without Km determination the reported IC50 is condition-specific.",
    "Biochemical inhibition of isolated TAK1 does not demonstrate cellular target engagement or viability effects; any cellular follow-up would require separate, target-specific causality experiments (e.g. pathway readout plus rescue/competition), not ATP viability alone.",
    "All numeric design parameters (top concentration, dilution factor, points, replicates, vehicle fraction, acceptance criteria) are explicitly labeled assumptions, not sourced facts."
  ]
}
